# Draft delivery lineage exported by the Proposal Workbench (BRSF software-development profile). Refine, then validate with the BRSF validator.

ex:Mission a backlog:Mission ; rdfs:label "Concert tickets on Bitcoin signet for campus events"@en ; backlog:hasMissionStatement "Help event organisers issue concert tickets on Bitcoin signet. Let each ticket holder prove ownership at the gate, transfer tickets at or below the original price with club approval, and keep them after the event. Help gate staff reject copied or used tickets and manage entry more easily." ; backlog:hasMissionOutcome "Gate staff can check an unused ticket within two seconds. The system rejects copied or used tickets and transfers above the original price. Ticket holders can keep tickets from attended events in their collection." ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_SessionDrafted .
ex:Lineage a backlog:Lineage ; backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 .
ex:Customer1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Campus music club"@en ; rdfs:comment "Customer (owner): Tickets with ownership checks, resale limits and quick entry."@en .
ex:EndUser1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Event organiser"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Club members who organise concerts. - Create events, set ticket rules and issue tickets. (three to four events a term, laptop browser)"@en .
ex:EndUser2 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Ticket holder"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Students and guests attending concerts. - Keep, transfer and show tickets on a phone. (a few events a term, phone)"@en .
ex:EndUser3 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Gate staff"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Club volunteers at the entrance. - Scan tickets and admit valid holders. (Each event, a few hundred scans per hour, phone)"@en .
