ex:D2 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Organiser page to create events and explain invalid rules."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D3 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Signet ticket script, minting and club-approved transfers."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D4 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Keep personal data off the chain."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_NonFunctional .
ex:D5 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Phone wallet with ticket transfers and a collection."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D6 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Gate scanner with signed challenges and results in under two seconds."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:X1 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Mainnet transactions and real bitcoin"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Use signet only, with no real bitcoin." .
ex:X2 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Taking ticket payments"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The club collects lira payments separately." .
ex:X3 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Stopping payments made outside the system"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The system cannot check cash or other outside payments. It uses the price both sides confirm." .
ex:X4 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Seat maps and reserved seating"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Use standing events with one ticket type." .
ex:G1 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Admit only holders of unused tickets"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Reduce copied tickets and queues." .
ex:G2 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Keep valid event and ticket records"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Transfers and collections need correct data." .
ex:G3 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Issue and transfer tickets under club rules"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Prevent transfers that break the resale rules." .
ex:G4 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Keep personal data off the chain"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Containment ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Protect holder privacy." .
ex:Spec a backlog:Specification ; backlog:hasSpecificationText "The organiser creates an event with a capacity, price and resale rules. SHACL checks these records. Each ticket is a signet output that needs both holder and club signatures. One week after the event, the holder can spend it alone. The phone wallet stores the holder's key. The club approves transfers only at or below the original price and allows at most three transfers. At the gate, the wallet signs a fresh challenge. The service checks ownership and whether the ticket was already used. Tickets remain in the holder's collection after the event." .
ex:Scen1 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given an unused ticket, when its wallet signs the gate challenge, then admit the holder within two seconds and record entry." .
ex:Scen2 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a copied ticket image, when it is scanned without the holder's key, then reject it and show a reason." .
ex:Scen3 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a transfer price twice the original price, when approval is requested, then refuse it and keep the current holder." .
ex:Scen4 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Boundary ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given three previous transfers, when a fourth is requested, then refuse it and explain the limit." .
ex:O1 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Invalid tickets admitted"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Number of copied or invalid tickets admitted per event." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "40" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease .
ex:O2 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Valid event and ticket records"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Percentage of records passing SHACL checks." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "100" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O3 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Transfers following the rules"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Percentage of signet transfers with club approval and a confirmed price at or below the original price." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "100" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O4 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Personal data on chain"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G4 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Number of outputs or witnesses containing data other than keys, signatures and the ticket script." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:Model_Activity a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ActivityDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Create and validate the event. Mint one ticket output per place and save its ID. After payment, assign the ticket to the buyer's wallet key. For a transfer, both sides confirm the price and the club checks the rules. At the gate, verify the wallet signature and record entry." .
ex:Model_Sequence a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_SequenceDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The organiser page sends an event to TicketAPI. The service validates it with pySHACL and stores it in Oxigraph. Bitcoin Core funds and signs the mint transaction. For transfers, the wallet signs a PSBT; the service checks the rules, adds the club signature and fee input, then broadcasts it. At the gate, the wallet signs a fresh nonce. The service checks ticket ownership and previous entry." .
ex:Model_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Event stores the date, venue, capacity and ResaleRule. The rule stores the price, resale cap and transfer limit. Ticket belongs to one Event and uses its mint outpoint as its ID. TicketOutput stores the current outpoint, holder key and script. Transfer links old and new outputs, price and club signature. CheckIn records the ticket, time and gate device. Each ticket has one current unspent output." .
